{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.BindingQbetaComplexVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.BindingQbetaComplexVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:QOU.MassEndomorphism.rotation_step","lean:module:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath"],"declarations":43,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.channel_casoratian_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.channel_casoratian_const","kind":"theorem","line":507,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L507-L522","doc":"**Channel-Casoratian invariance (proved).**  Along a `recurrence_invol_descent`\nladder — one three-term recurrence `V₂ = c·V₁ − V₀` with a bar-even\nmultiplier — the Casoratian of the two parity channels (bar-even/binding\nagainst bar-odd/`𝔔_β`) is *invariant*: constant multiplier ⇒ `B = −1` ⇒\n`W' = W`.  A measured drift of the physical channel Casoratian therefore\nreads directly as the `k`-dependence of the AW coefficient `B_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.casoratian_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.casoratian_step","kind":"theorem","line":498,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L498-L505","doc":"**Casoratian descent (proved).**  If two sequences satisfy the SAME\nthree-term step `X₂ = A·X₁ + B·X₀`, their Casoratian\n`W = X₀·Y₁ − X₁·Y₀` transports by one step as `W' = −B·W`.\nNo hypothesis on `A` is needed — the multiplier cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chM_eigencolumn_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chM_eigencolumn_iff","kind":"theorem","line":458,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L458-L480","doc":"**Eigencolumns of the free-endpoint channel operator are exactly the\nq-Hermite three-term rows**: `(M v) n = θ·v n` unfolds to the seed row\n`(1−q)·v 1 = θ·v 0` and the generic row\n`(1−q^{n+2})·v_{n+2} + v_n = θ·v_{n+1}` — the `evenStep` shape with\ndiagonal off.  Connects `chM` to `IsEigencolumn`/`overlapColumn`\nwithout a unit assumption on the super-diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chM_eq_L_add_R","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chM_eq_L_add_R","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L454-L456","doc":"The channel operator is the shift-split sum (definitional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chLR_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chLR_comm","kind":"theorem","line":435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L435-L452","doc":"**The q-oscillator commutator (degenerate AW(3), proved):**\n`L ∘ R − R ∘ L = (1 − q) · Q`.  This is the concrete channel-operator\nform of Zhedanov's algebra at the q-Hermite bottom; the odd channel\nsatisfies the same relation at `σ q` by instantiation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chLQ_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chLQ_rel","kind":"theorem","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L427-L433","doc":"**q-commutation of lowering with grading**: `L ∘ Q = q · (Q ∘ L)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chQR_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chQR_rel","kind":"theorem","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L417-L425","doc":"**q-commutation of grading with raising**: `Q ∘ R = q · (R ∘ Q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chM","kind":"def","line":411,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L411-L415","doc":"The channel tridiagonal operator at the q-Hermite bottom:\nmultiplication by `2x` in the channel basis is `M = L + R`\n(diagonal term zero — the free endpoint of `AWDeformationPath`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chQ","kind":"def","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L407-L409","doc":"Grading (diagonal) operator: `(Q v) n = q^n · v n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chL","kind":"def","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L402-L405","doc":"Lowering (super-diagonal) channel operator with the even-channel\ncoefficient: `(L v) n = (1 − q^{n+1}) · v (n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.chR","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.chR","kind":"def","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L397-L400","doc":"Raising (sub-diagonal) channel operator: `(R v) 0 = 0`, `(R v)(n+1) = v n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.channel_ladders","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.AWDeformationPath.channel_ladders","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L350-L362","doc":"Derived (proved, conditional on the class): the σ-even (binding) and\nσ-odd (`𝔔_β`) ladders each satisfy the SAME three-term recurrence —\nthe two channels are the two parities of the one deformation-path\nladder.  Direct application of `recurrence_invol_descent`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.row_three_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.row_three_term","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L308-L324","doc":"Derived (proved, conditional on the class): the **rows** of the overlap\nmatrix satisfy the dual three-term recurrence — the second\ntridiagonalisation that makes the pair \"Leonard\".  One proof serves\nboth channels, per `recurrence_invol_descent`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.duality","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L305-L305","doc":"Leonard self-duality of the overlap matrix: `p_n(θ_m) = p*_m(θ*_n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.θstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.θstar","kind":"def","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L303-L303","doc":"dual eigenvalue sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.dualC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.dualC","kind":"def","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L301-L301","doc":"dual sub-diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.dualB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.dualB","kind":"def","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L299-L299","doc":"dual diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.dualA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.dualA","kind":"def","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L297-L297","doc":"dual super-diagonal (units). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L295-L295","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ChannelLeonardDuality","kind":"class","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L285-L306","doc":"**Leonard-duality conjecture for the channel pair (§3b class;\nconjecture — no instance is provided).**  The overlap matrix of the\nchannel tridiagonal data is *self-dual*: there exist dual tridiagonal\ndata and dual eigenvalues with `p_n(θ_m) = p*_m(θ*_n)` — the defining\nproperty of a Leonard / tridiagonal pair.  By Terwilliger's\nclassification this forces the overlap coefficients into the\nAskey–Wilson (q-Racah) family: *the two channels are a Leonard pair\nand the AW polynomials are the rotation between them.*  Fields carry\nthe conjecture's inputs (the dual data and the quantified duality),\nper §3b-tax content rules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.eigencolumn_eq_overlap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.eigencolumn_eq_overlap","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L236-L283","doc":"**Overlap coefficients are the orthogonal polynomials (rotation-matrix\ntheorem), sorry-free.**  Any `θ`-eigencolumn of the tridiagonal channel\noperator is `v 0 · p_n(θ)`: the intertwiner between the channel basis\nand the spectral basis is *forced* to have orthogonal-polynomial\nentries.  This is the provable half of \"the AW polynomials are the\nrotation between the two channels\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.IsEigencolumn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.IsEigencolumn","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L228-L234","doc":"`v` is a `θ`-eigencolumn of the tridiagonal (channel-basis) operator\nwith sub/diag/super data `(c, b, a)`: the seed row plus the generic\nthree-term row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.overlapColumn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.overlapColumn","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L216-L226","doc":"The overlap (\"rotation-matrix\") column: the orthogonal-polynomial\nsequence of the tridiagonal data `(a, b, c)` evaluated at the spectral\nvalue `θ`.  Super-diagonal entries `a` are units so the recursion is\ndivision-free-normalisable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.evenStep_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.evenStep_map","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L182-L189","doc":"The bar involution transports an even step to an even step at the\nconjugated data (`σ` a ring hom: coefficients map through). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.measured_complex_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.measured_complex_volume","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L151-L159","doc":"Under the physical-match class, the measured observables reconstruct\nthe complex defect: `𝔈_bind^obs + i·𝔔_β^obs = 𝔙`.  Now immediate from the\nsingle `volume_match` + the definitional unification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.qbeta_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.qbeta_match","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L145-L147","doc":"Measured Q-value matches `Im 𝔙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.binding_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.binding_match","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L142-L144","doc":"Measured binding matches `Re 𝔙` (derived from the single `volume_match`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.qbeta_measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.qbeta_measured","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L139-L140","doc":"Measured β-decay Q-value `𝔔_β^obs := Im 𝔙_obs`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.binding_measured","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.binding_measured","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L137-L138","doc":"Measured binding `𝔈_bind^obs := Re 𝔙_obs`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.volume_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.volume_match","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L132-L132","doc":"the single physical-match hypothesis: `𝔙_obs = E₀·(defect)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.measured_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.measured_volume","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L130-L130","doc":"the **measured complex volume** `𝔙_obs = 𝔈_bind^obs + i·𝔔_β^obs ∈ ℂ`\n(binding as Re, β-decay Q-value as Im — one observable, two shadows). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.trDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.trDefect","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L127-L127","doc":"the complexified convolution-defect `tr_M((Π_free−1)∘𝓜)(K) ∈ ℂ` (fibre-level). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.E0","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L125-L125","doc":"substrate energy scale `E₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.ComplexVolumeMatch","kind":"class","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L116-L132","doc":"The physical-match conjecture (AGENTS.md §3b-cond class): the\n*measured* complex volume of a composite `K` — the **single** observable\n`𝔙_obs = 𝔈_bind^obs + i·𝔔_β^obs` — equals `𝔙(K)` at a single\nnormalisation.  One hypothesis (`volume_match`), not two parallel arms:\nbinding and `Q_β` are the Re/Im of *one* measured object, matched to the\nRe/Im of *one* fibre object.  This is the conjectural input; the\nunification theorem above is proved unconditionally. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:binding-qbeta-complex-volume","label":"conj:binding-qbeta-complex-volume","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.complex_volume_unification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.complex_volume_unification","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L94-L102","doc":"**The complex-volume unification (definitional, PROVED, sorry-free).**\nBinding (Re) and β-decay (Im) reconstruct the one complex fibre\nobject `𝔙`: `𝔈_bind + i·𝔔_β = 𝔙`.  Mass and binding are no longer two\nstories — they are the two parities of one complex volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.Qbeta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.Qbeta","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L91-L92","doc":"β-decay `𝔔_β := Im 𝔙` — the bar-odd / Chern–Simons channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.binding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.binding","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L89-L90","doc":"Binding `𝔈_bind := Re 𝔙` — the bar-even / volume channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.fibreDefect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.fibreDefect","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L86-L87","doc":"The complex fibre observable `𝔙 = E₀·tr_M((Π_free−1)∘𝓜) ∈ ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.recurrence_invol_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.recurrence_invol_descent","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L70-L80","doc":"**Recurrence descent — the `c_k`-ladder mechanism, generic.** A\nthree-term recurrence `𝔙ₚ = c·𝔙ₖ − 𝔙ₘ` with a **bar-even** multiplier\n`c` (`σ c = c`, the `2cosh η` analogue) yields the binding (`σ`-even)\nAND `𝔔_β` (`σ`-odd) recurrences from the *single* ring proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.invol_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.invol_descent","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L62-L68","doc":"**Involution descent.** One ring identity `x = w` yields BOTH the\nbar-even (binding) and bar-odd (`𝔔_β`) identities at once — the\n`[CommRing R]`-generic form of \"prove on `𝔙` once, read off both\nchannels\" (no `ℂ`, no `/2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.barParity_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.barParity_diff","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L59-L60","doc":"`σ`-even − `σ`-odd reconstructs `2·σx`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.barParity_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.barParity_sum","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/binding-qbeta-complex-volume.lean#L56-L57","doc":"`σ`-even + `σ`-odd reconstructs `2x` (`(x+σx) + (x−σx) = 2x`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}